# Auto commit & push

When finishing a meaningful change set in this repo (features, fixes, PDF/layout, releases), **commit and push to `origin` without waiting for the user to ask again**.

## When to commit
- After completing the user’s requested work (or a coherent slice of it)
- Include related files only — no secrets (`.env`, credentials, private keys)
- Skip empty commits; skip if the user explicitly said not to commit

## How
1. Follow the repo’s git commit protocol (status, diff, log, stage, HEREDOC message, status)
2. Push with `git push -u origin HEAD` when the branch should update GitHub
3. If a GitHub Release / Update asset is needed for Windows or Android, publish with `scripts/publish_release.ps1` (bump version when shipping user-facing changes)

## Commit message style
Match recent history: concise, imperative, focus on why (e.g. “Tighten piece-count field spacing on wide Windows layouts.”).
